          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What quality standards do you maintain for bikini production?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We maintain OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification for all bikini fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances. We conduct chlorine resistance testing for fabrics intended for pool use, UV protection testing for sun safety, and stretch recovery testing to ensure fit retention. Our construction includes reinforced stitching at stress points and secure elastic application. All bikinis undergo wash testing to verify color fastness and dimensional stability. These standards ensure our bikinis withstand the demanding conditions of swimwear use."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does bikini production take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Standard production timeline is 35-45 days from fabric receipt for basic bikini styles. Complex styles with specialized features typically require 40-50 days. Custom fabric development adds 15-20 days. Sampling takes 15-20 days before bulk production approval. Intricate designs with multiple components or specialized construction may require 50-60 days production time. We recommend planning 65-80 days total from initial inquiry to delivery for first-time orders including sampling and production."
