  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Introduction</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Bikini Manufacturer for Swimwear and Beachwear Brands</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>As a specialized bikini manufacturer based in Bangladesh, SDF Clothing understands that swimwear requires exceptional durability, stretch recovery, and resistance to harsh environmental conditions. The bikini market encompasses diverse needs from basic beachwear to performance swimwear, requiring expertise in stretch fabrics and secure construction. Our facility delivers on these requirements with minimum orders of 300 pieces, making professional bikini manufacturing accessible to emerging brands and established labels expanding their swimwear collections.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a competitive sourcing destination for swimwear, combining cost advantages with developing expertise in stretch garment production. Our bikini production leverages Bangladesh's textile ecosystem, offering international brands access to skilled labor, established supply chains for nylon/spandex and performance fabrics, and comprehensive manufacturing capabilities. The 300-piece minimum enables brands to test different bikini styles and fabric options without committing to large inventory positions, reducing risk while accessing factory-direct pricing.</p>
        
        <p>Our bikini manufacturing addresses the specific requirements of swimwear: stretch fabrics with excellent recovery to maintain fit through repeated use, chlorine resistance for pool durability, UV protection for sun safety, secure construction that withstands saltwater and sunscreen exposure, and designs that balance aesthetic appeal with functional performance. We work with nylon/spandex, polyester/spandex, and recycled materials to meet various performance requirements and sustainability goals while maintaining OEKO-TEX certification for chemical safety.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Product Range</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">What We Manufacture</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our bikini production encompasses multiple styles designed for different preferences, body types, and market segments. Each style maintains our commitment to quality fabrics and secure construction while offering distinct aesthetic and functional characteristics. We manufacture all styles from 300 pieces minimum, with the ability to mix styles within larger orders for comprehensive swimwear collections.</p>
        
        <p>Triangle bikinis represent the classic bikini style, featuring triangular cups with strings or thin straps at the neck and back. We produce traditional triangle bikinis with adjustable ties, fixed-strap triangle bikinis for security, and variations with different cup coverage levels. Triangle bikinis typically use lightweight stretch fabrics in the 180-200 GSM range. The simple construction makes triangle bikinis cost-effective swimwear staples. Triangle bikinis are versatile and popular across multiple market segments, from beach essentials to fashion-forward collections.</p>
        
        <p>Bandeau bikinis feature strapless tube-style tops that provide smooth tan lines without shoulder straps. We produce basic bandeau bikinis with elasticized tops, bandeau bikinis with removable straps for versatility, and bandeau styles with center ruching for enhanced fit. Bandeau bikinis require careful construction to ensure secure fit without straps, often incorporating silicone gripper elastic at the top and bottom. Bandeau bikinis use medium-weight fabrics in the 190-210 GSM range for structure. Bandeau bikinis are popular for their clean lines and tan-line-free styling.</p>
        
        <p>Halter neck bikinis feature tops with straps that tie behind the neck, providing lift and support. We produce halter bikinis with classic triangle cups, halter styles with underwire for additional support, and variations with different neck tie configurations. The halter configuration provides adjustable fit and enhanced bust support compared to strapless styles. Halter bikinis use fabrics in the 180-210 GSM range depending on support requirements. The halter neck is particularly popular for customers seeking additional support and lift in bikini tops.</p>
        
        <p>High-waisted bikinis feature bottoms with waistbands that sit above the natural waistline, offering retro styling and tummy coverage. We produce high-waisted bikini bottoms in various leg opening widths from modest to cheeky, with different waistband heights from mid-rise to very high-waisted. High-waisted styles often feature vintage-inspired details like high-cut legs and moderate coverage. These styles use fabrics in the 190-220 GSM range for structure and support. High-waisted bikinis have experienced significant popularity in recent years as part of the retro fashion trend.</p>
        
        <p>Sports bikinis are designed for active use, incorporating performance features for swimming, water sports, and beach activities. We produce sports bikini tops with racerback configurations for enhanced shoulder mobility, sports bikini bottoms with secure fits for active movement, and performance styles with compression support. Sports bikinis often feature higher necklines, wider straps, and moderate coverage for security during activity. These styles use performance fabrics with chlorine resistance and UV protection in the 200-220 GSM range. Sports bikinis bridge the gap between fashion swimwear and performance athletic wear.</p>
        
        <p>Push-up bikinis incorporate padding and construction techniques to enhance bust appearance. We produce push-up bikini tops with removable padding, push-up styles with underwire for additional lift, and variations with different levels of enhancement. The construction requires careful pattern work to ensure padding stays in place and provides natural enhancement. Push-up bikinis use medium-weight fabrics in the 190-210 GSM range to support padding without compromising stretch. Push-up bikinis are popular in markets seeking enhanced silhouettes and more structured bikini styling.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Style</th>
              <th>Fabric GSM</th>
              <th>Key Features</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Triangle Bikini</td>
