      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our bikini manufacturing follows a structured process designed to ensure consistent quality, fabric performance, and construction durability. The process typically spans 65-80 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 50-65 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Bikinis require particular attention to stretch recovery and chlorine resistance to withstand demanding swimwear conditions.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with specification review, where we analyze your requirements including fabric preferences (nylon/spandex, polyester/spandex, recycled), style type, size chart, and performance requirements. Our team provides feedback on technical feasibility and may suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining design intent. This stage takes 2-3 days and ensures technical alignment before sampling begins. For bikinis, we pay particular attention to fabric stretch requirements and elastic specifications.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and development follows specification review, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. Bikini fabrics undergo rigorous testing for stretch recovery, chlorine resistance, UV protection, and color fastness before approval. We test fabrics for durability against saltwater, sunscreen, and repeated washing. All fabrics must meet OEKO-TEX Standard 100 requirements for swimwear safety. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors or performance properties, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage for testing and approval.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development for bikinis takes 15-20 days for basic styles and 20-25 days for complex designs with specialized features. Initial samples focus on construction and basic fit, with subsequent samples refining fit details, fabric performance, and finish quality. We provide detailed measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications and conduct stretch recovery testing to verify fit retention. Bikini samples require particular attention to elastic application and seam strength. You may request multiple sample rounds to perfect the design.</p>
        
        <p>Performance testing is a critical step in bikini sampling that we conduct on all samples. We test stretch recovery to ensure fabric returns to original shape after stretching, evaluate chlorine resistance for pool durability, verify UV protection ratings for sun safety, and assess color fastness against saltwater and sunscreen exposure. For sports bikinis, we conduct additional testing for secure fit during activity. This performance-focused testing ensures that the final product meets the demanding requirements of swimwear use and provides customers with reliable performance.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading for bikinis requires careful attention to proportional scaling, particularly for cup sizing and bottom fit. The relationship between various measurements must be maintained through grading to ensure consistent fit across sizes. Our pattern makers use graded measurement systems that account for these relationships, producing size sets from XS to XL that maintain proportional fit appropriate for each size. Grading takes 3-5 days for basic styles and 5-7 days for complex designs with multiple components. Grading includes verification of cup sizing consistency and bottom fit proportions.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production for bikinis spans 35-45 days from fabric receipt for basic styles. Complex designs with specialized features typically require 40-50 days. Cutting is performed with attention to grain direction for optimal stretch behavior. Sewing lines are staffed by operators trained in swimwear construction, with particular expertise in stretch fabric handling, elastic application, and reinforced stitching. Quality checkpoints at each sewing operation verify seam integrity, elastic security, and construction accuracy with performance focus.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, with additional testing for bikini-specific criteria. Inspection includes measurement verification against graded size charts, stretch recovery testing on random samples, and construction quality verification with particular attention to elastic security and seam strength. We also conduct chlorine resistance testing and color fastness verification. Detailed inspection reports with photos are provided before shipment, and any performance-related defects result in immediate rectification.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to bikini performance, affecting stretch recovery, durability, chlorine resistance, and sun protection. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different use cases and performance requirements. All fabrics are certified safe for swimwear through OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification.</p>
        
        <p>Nylon/spandex blends are the traditional choice for swimwear, providing excellent stretch recovery, durability, and resistance to saltwater and chlorine. Nylon/spandex typically ranges from 180-220 GSM with spandex content between 15-20% for optimal stretch and recovery. Nylon offers superior strength compared to polyester, making it ideal for swimwear that must withstand demanding conditions. The fabric has excellent color retention and resists fading from sun exposure. Nylon/spandex is our recommendation for premium swimwear where durability and performance are priorities.</p>
        
        <p>Polyester/spandex blends offer color retention and cost efficiency, making them popular for fashion swimwear. Polyester/spandex typically ranges from 180-220 GSM with similar spandex content to nylon blends. Polyester offers superior color fastness and resistance to fading compared to nylon, making it ideal for vibrant prints and colors. Polyester also resists chlorine damage better than nylon, though it may have slightly less stretch recovery. Polyester/spandex is ideal for fashion-forward swimwear where color vibrancy and print quality are priorities.</p>
        
        <p>Recycled polyester/spandex certified by GRS (Global Recycled Standard) provides sustainable synthetic options for eco-conscious swimwear. Recycled polyester is produced from post-consumer plastic bottles or post-industrial waste, reducing environmental impact compared to virgin polyester. Recycled polyester/spandex maintains the same performance characteristics as virgin polyester while offering sustainability credentials. Recycled materials cost approximately 10-15% more than conventional polyester but enable sustainability claims that appeal to environmentally conscious consumers. GRS certification provides verification of recycled content.</p>
        
        <p>ECONYL regenerated nylon is a premium sustainable option produced from reclaimed nylon waste including fishing nets and carpet fluff. ECONYL offers the same performance as virgin nylon with significantly reduced environmental impact. The regenerated nylon maintains excellent stretch recovery, chlorine resistance, and durability while diverting waste from oceans and landfills. ECONYL costs approximately 20-25% more than conventional nylon but provides premium sustainability credentials that appeal to brands seeking leadership in environmental responsibility.</p>
        
        <p>Performance fabrics incorporate additional features beyond basic stretch and durability. These fabrics may include UV protection ratings (UPF 50+) for sun safety, chlorine resistance treatments for extended pool use, quick-drying properties for comfort, and antimicrobial treatments for odor resistance. Performance fabrics typically range from 200-220 GSM to provide additional structure for performance features. These fabrics are ideal for sports bikinis and swimwear intended for frequent use in demanding conditions.</p>
        
        <p>All swimwear fabrics undergo OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification testing for harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, formaldehyde, and other chemicals. This certification is essential for swimwear due to prolonged skin contact and exposure to sun and water which can increase chemical absorption. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each fabric lot, enabling you to substantiate safety claims in your marketing materials and meet retailer requirements for swimwear safety certification.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Fabric</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Nylon/Spandex</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Durable, stretch recovery, chlorine resistant</td>
              <td>Premium swimwear, durability</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Polyester/Spandex</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Color fast, cost efficient, vibrant prints</td>
              <td>Fashion swimwear, prints</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Recycled Polyester/Spandex</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Sustainable, GRS certified, performance</td>
              <td>Eco-conscious, sustainability</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>ECONYL Regenerated Nylon</td>
              <td>180-220</td>
              <td>Premium sustainable, ocean waste, performance</td>
              <td>Premium sustainability, leadership</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Performance Fabrics</td>
              <td>200-220</td>
              <td>UV protection, chlorine resistant, quick-dry</td>
              <td>Sports swimwear, active use</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
          <caption>All fabrics OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certified for swimwear safety.</caption>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__Label">Bangladesh Advantage</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Why Source Bikinis from Bangladesh</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a competitive sourcing destination for swimwear, combining cost advantages with developing expertise in stretch garment production. The country's garment industry includes numerous factories focused on activewear and stretch garments, with established supply chains for nylon/spandex and performance fabrics. This specialization, combined with competitive labor costs, makes Bangladesh an attractive option for bikini manufacturing.</p>
        
        <p>Labor costs in Bangladesh are significantly lower than in China, Vietnam, or Turkey, translating to 15-25% cost savings on finished bikinis. However, the cost advantage does not come at the expense of quality. The Bangladeshi garment industry has developed particular expertise in stretch garment production, with operators skilled in handling spandex fabrics, constructing elasticized garments, and maintaining consistent quality on stretch materials. Our facility conducts regular training programs to ensure operators are proficient in the latest swimwear construction techniques.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's textile infrastructure includes knitting mills capable of producing nylon/spandex and polyester/spandex blends suitable for swimwear. The country has invested in circular knitting capacity for stretch fabrics, reducing reliance on imported materials for basic bikini styles. This local sourcing reduces lead times and logistics costs compared to countries that rely entirely on imported fabrics. Our relationships with local knitting mills ensure priority allocation and consistent quality for swimwear fabrics. For specialized fabrics or custom weights, we maintain relationships with international fabric suppliers.</p>
        
        <p>The country's export infrastructure includes experienced freight forwarders, customs brokers, and documentation specialists familiar with garment export requirements. Shipments from Bangladesh to major markets are routine, with multiple weekly sailings to Europe and North America. Ocean freight is particularly cost-effective for bikinis given the lightweight nature of the garments, allowing efficient container utilization. The established export infrastructure reduces the risk of delays and documentation errors that can occur with less experienced sourcing locations.</p>
        
        <p>Social compliance and workplace safety have improved significantly in Bangladesh's garment industry following comprehensive reforms after 2013. Our facility holds BSCI certification, demonstrating adherence to international labor standards including fair wages, reasonable working hours, and safe working conditions. These certifications are increasingly important to consumers and retailers who prioritize ethical sourcing. The improved compliance environment reduces reputational risk for brands sourcing from Bangladesh.</p>
        
        <p>Duty-free access to European markets through the Everything But Arms (EBA) arrangement provides Bangladesh garments with preferential tariff treatment, reducing import costs for EU customers. Similar preferential access exists for other markets including Canada, Australia, and Japan. This duty advantage can significantly impact landed costs for bikinis, which are subject to standard garment duty rates in many markets. For brands targeting EU distribution, the duty savings can offset other costs and improve overall margins.</p>
        
        <p>The Bangladesh garment industry has developed specialized expertise in stretch garment production, which directly translates to bikini manufacturing. Handling spandex fabrics, constructing elasticized garments, and producing swimwear that maintains performance through repeated use are well-established skills in the country's workforce. This specialized expertise reduces the learning curve for new bikini styles and ensures consistent quality across production runs. The industry's experience with international activewear brands also means that performance expectations are well-understood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">International Shipping</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Shipping to UK, USA, Australia & EU</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We ship bikinis to major international markets including the United Kingdom, United States, Australia, and European Union countries. Each market has specific requirements for documentation, duties, and shipping timelines that we navigate routinely. Our experience with international bikini shipments ensures your goods arrive on time and with proper documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Shipments to the United Kingdom typically take 30-35 days by ocean freight, including transit time and customs clearance. Air freight options reduce this to 7-10 days at significantly higher cost. The UK applies import duties on garments from Bangladesh, though rates vary by garment type and fabric composition. Bikinis typically fall under specific HS codes for swimwear. We provide accurate classification and valuation to ensure proper duty calculation. Post-Brexit documentation requirements are handled to ensure smooth customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>United States shipments take 25-30 days by ocean freight to West Coast ports and 35-40 days to East Coast ports. Air freight takes 5-7 days to major US airports. The US maintains normal trade relations with Bangladesh, with standard MFN duty rates applying to bikinis. The US has specific labeling requirements for garments including fiber content in English and country of origin. We ensure all labels meet US Federal Trade Commission requirements. US customs compliance is handled through proper documentation and accurate classification.</p>
        
        <p>Australia shipments take 20-25 days by ocean freight to major ports including Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane. Air freight takes 7-10 days. Australia maintains a free trade agreement with Bangladesh that eliminates duties on many garments when rules of origin are met. We ensure our production processes meet these origin requirements to qualify for duty-free entry. Australia's strict biosecurity requirements are addressed through proper packaging and documentation to prevent clearance delays.</p>
        
        <p>European Union shipments benefit from duty-free access under the Everything But Arms arrangement. Ocean freight takes 28-32 days to Northern European ports and 32-38 days to Southern European ports. Air freight takes 5-8 days. EU countries require specific documentation including certificates of origin, commercial invoices with detailed descriptions, and conformity declarations for certain materials. The EU also has specific requirements for textile labeling including fiber content percentages and care instructions in the language of the destination country.</p>
        
        <p>Documentation for all markets includes commercial invoices, packing lists, bills of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. For bikinis, this may include certificates for recycled materials when applicable. We provide all documentation in English and can arrange for translations if required by specific markets. Our documentation is prepared to meet both customs requirements and your internal accounting needs, with clear descriptions and accurate valuations.</p>
        
        <p>Incoterms can be structured according to your preferences, including FOB (Free On Board) Bangladesh for maximum control, CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) to destination port for convenience, or DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) for complete door-to-door service. For bikinis, we typically recommend FOB for experienced importers, as the cost savings on ocean freight for lightweight garments make FOB economically advantageous. CIF and DDP options are available for brands seeking simplified logistics or those new to international sourcing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Certifications</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Quality Standards & Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Quality assurance and certification are fundamental to our bikini manufacturing process. Swimwear requires particular attention to performance certification due to the demanding conditions of use. We maintain multiple certifications that verify our commitment to quality, sustainability, and social responsibility.</p>
        
        <p>OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification applies to all our bikini fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, formaldehyde, and other chemicals. This certification is essential for swimwear due to prolonged skin contact and exposure to sun and water which can increase chemical absorption. OEKO-TEX testing covers all fabric components including base materials, threads, trims, and elastic. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each material lot, enabling you to substantiate safety claims in your marketing materials.</p>
        
        <p>GRS (Global Recycled Standard) certification applies to our recycled polyester swimwear fabrics, verifying recycled content and ensuring traceability throughout the supply chain. GRS certification covers environmental and social criteria for recycled material production, including wastewater treatment, chemical restrictions, and labor practices. If you choose recycled materials for your bikinis, GRS certification provides credible substantiation for sustainability claims and is increasingly required by major retailers for recycled content products.</p>
        
        <p>BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative) certification verifies our adherence to international labor standards including fair wages, reasonable working hours, prohibition of child labor, and safe working conditions. BSCI audits are conducted by independent third-party auditors and cover all aspects of social compliance. This certification is important for brands that prioritize ethical sourcing and need to demonstrate supply chain responsibility to stakeholders and consumers increasingly concerned about labor practices.</p>
        
        <p>ISO 9001 certification applies to our quality management system, ensuring consistent processes for production and quality control. ISO 9001 requires documented procedures for all critical processes, regular internal audits, and continuous improvement. This certification provides assurance that our quality systems are systematic and repeatable, reducing variability between production runs. For bikinis, this means consistent performance, fabric quality, and construction across orders.</p>
        
        <p>Internal quality control processes supplement these certifications with day-to-day assurance specific to bikini production. We conduct in-line inspections during production, measuring garments at critical checkpoints to verify dimensional accuracy. Final inspection includes stretch recovery testing, chlorine resistance verification, color fastness testing, and visual inspection of stitching and elastic application. We maintain records of all testing results, enabling traceability if issues arise after delivery.</p>
      </div>
