        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">How to Get Started</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Starting your bikini production with SDF Clothing follows a structured process designed to ensure your performance and quality requirements are met from the outset. The process begins with providing detailed specifications, after which we guide you through sampling, performance testing, and production.</p>
        
        <p>Step one is to submit your technical specifications through our contact form or email. Essential information for bikinis includes: fabric preference (nylon/spandex, polyester/spandex, recycled), style type, size chart or target market sizing, performance requirements (chlorine resistance, UV protection), target quantity per style and color, and desired delivery timeline. If you have technical drawings, photos of reference samples, or existing products you want to replicate, include these for clarity.</p>
        
        <p>Step two involves our technical review and quotation process. Within 24-48 hours of receiving your specifications, we provide a detailed quotation including fabric costs, production costs, sampling costs, and estimated shipping costs. The quotation specifies lead times for sampling and production, minimum order quantities, and payment terms. For bikinis, we clarify performance testing requirements and ensure all fabrics meet OEKO-TEX Standard 100. You may request revisions to the quotation to adjust specifications to meet budget targets.</p>
        
        <p>Step three is sample development and approval. After quotation acceptance, we proceed with sample development, typically taking 15-20 days for basic styles and 20-25 days for complex designs. Samples are shipped to you for review, and we provide detailed measurement reports. For bikinis, we recommend performance testing samples to verify stretch recovery, chlorine resistance, and overall performance. You may approve samples as-is, request modifications to fit or fabric, or proceed with additional sample rounds.</p>
        
        <p>Step four is production confirmation. Once samples are approved and performance is verified, we require a deposit to confirm production and initiate fabric procurement. Standard terms are 30% deposit with order confirmation and 70% before shipment. Production begins after deposit receipt and fabric availability is confirmed. We provide a production schedule with key milestones including cutting completion, sewing completion, and expected shipment date. Throughout production, we provide status updates.</p>
        
        <p>Step five is final inspection and shipment. Before shipment, we conduct final quality inspection using AQL standards with additional testing for bikini-specific criteria including performance verification. We provide an inspection report for your review. Once inspection is approved, we finalize packaging with your branding elements and prepare shipping documentation including all required certificates. Balance payment is required before release of shipping documents. We provide all necessary documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Throughout the process, our team provides technical guidance on bikini construction, fabric selection, and performance optimization. We understand that swimwear requires exceptional performance and quality to maintain customer satisfaction in demanding conditions. Clear communication about performance expectations and requirements helps us deliver products that meet international swimwear standards.</p>
      </div>
