      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order quantity for bikinis?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Our minimum order quantity for custom bikinis is 300 pieces per style. This minimum allows you to access factory-direct pricing while testing market response with manageable inventory. The 300-piece minimum can be distributed across sizes within a single colorway. For bikini sets counted as single styles, the minimum applies to the complete set. Lower quantities are available for sampling and prototype development at higher per-piece costs for brands requiring smaller initial runs.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What fabric options do you offer for bikinis?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">We offer nylon/spandex blends for durability and stretch (180-220 GSM), polyester/spandex for color retention and cost efficiency (180-220 GSM), recycled polyester/spandex certified by GRS for sustainability (180-220 GSM), and high-performance fabrics with UV protection and chlorine resistance. All fabrics are OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certified for swimwear safety. Fabric selection depends on intended use (pool, beach, competition), performance requirements, and sustainability goals, with chlorine-resistant options for frequent pool use.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What bikini styles can you manufacture?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">We manufacture triangle bikinis with classic styling, bandeau bikinis for strapless wear, halter neck bikinis with supportive necklines, high-waisted bikinis for retro styling, sports bikinis for active use, and push-up bikinis with enhanced support. All styles can be customized with various top and bottom combinations. We produce both bikini separates and matching sets. Custom style development is available with technical specifications. Each style offers distinct aesthetic and functional characteristics for different market segments.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Do you offer sustainable bikini options?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Yes. We offer recycled polyester/spandex certified by GRS for sustainable synthetic options, and we can source ECONYL regenerated nylon from ocean waste for premium sustainability. All sustainable options maintain the same quality and performance as conventional fabrics. Recycled materials cost approximately 10-15% more than conventional polyester but enable sustainability claims that appeal to eco-conscious consumers. We provide full GRS certification documentation for marketing substantiation and retailer compliance requirements.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What quality standards do you maintain for bikini production?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">We maintain OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification for all bikini fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances. We conduct chlorine resistance testing for fabrics intended for pool use, UV protection testing for sun safety, and stretch recovery testing to ensure fit retention. Our construction includes reinforced stitching at stress points and secure elastic application. All bikinis undergo wash testing to verify color fastness and dimensional stability. These standards ensure our bikinis withstand the demanding conditions of swimwear use.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does bikini production take?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">Standard production timeline is 35-45 days from fabric receipt for basic bikini styles. Complex styles with specialized features typically require 40-50 days. Custom fabric development adds 15-20 days. Sampling takes 15-20 days before bulk production approval. Intricate designs with multiple components or specialized construction may require 50-60 days production time. We recommend planning 65-80 days total from initial inquiry to delivery for first-time orders including sampling and production.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
